A lookup that returns the first row's value or a default, written with IIf.
IIf evaluates both value arguments, so the element is read when the query
matched nothing too, and the call raises instead of returning the default
(verified on STARLIMS 12, issue #372). diag.iif_guard_ineffective reports
the read behind an Empty test, behind a Len test, and a member read behind
a NIL test. The last procedure is the fix: the test as an :IF.
-- input.ssl --
:PROCEDURE GetOwnerName;
:PARAMETERS sSampleId;
:DECLARE aRows;
aRows := SQLExecute("SELECT OwnerName FROM Samples WHERE SampleID = ?sSampleId?");
:RETURN IIf(Empty(aRows), "", aRows[1, 1]);
:ENDPROC;

:PROCEDURE FirstTestCode;
:PARAMETERS aTests;
:RETURN IIf(Len(aTests) > 0, Upper(aTests[1]), "NONE");
:ENDPROC;

:PROCEDURE OwnerLabel;
:PARAMETERS oOwner;
:RETURN IIf(oOwner == NIL, "Unassigned", oOwner:displayName);
:ENDPROC;

:PROCEDURE GetOwnerNameSafely;
:PARAMETERS sSampleId;
:DECLARE aRows, sOwner;
aRows := SQLExecute("SELECT OwnerName FROM Samples WHERE SampleID = ?sSampleId?");
sOwner := "";
:IF !Empty(aRows);
sOwner := aRows[1, 1];
:ENDIF;
:RETURN sOwner;
:ENDPROC;
-- format --
:PROCEDURE GetOwnerName;
	:PARAMETERS sSampleId;
	:DECLARE aRows;

	aRows := SQLExecute("SELECT OwnerName FROM Samples WHERE SampleID = ?sSampleId?");

	:RETURN IIf(Empty(aRows), "", aRows[1, 1]);
:ENDPROC;

:PROCEDURE FirstTestCode;
	:PARAMETERS aTests;

	:RETURN IIf(Len(aTests) > 0, Upper(aTests[1]), "NONE");
:ENDPROC;

:PROCEDURE OwnerLabel;
	:PARAMETERS oOwner;

	:RETURN IIf(oOwner == NIL, "Unassigned", oOwner:displayName);
:ENDPROC;

:PROCEDURE GetOwnerNameSafely;
	:PARAMETERS sSampleId;
	:DECLARE aRows, sOwner;

	aRows := SQLExecute("SELECT OwnerName FROM Samples WHERE SampleID = ?sSampleId?");
	sOwner := "";

	:IF !Empty(aRows);
		sOwner := aRows[1, 1];
	:ENDIF;

	:RETURN sOwner;
:ENDPROC;
-- diagnostics --
5:31-5:42 warning iif_guard_ineffective: IIf evaluates both value arguments, so aRows[1, 1] is read even when aRows is empty, which raises an error. Make the test an :IF and read the value inside it.
10:36-10:45 warning iif_guard_ineffective: IIf evaluates both value arguments, so aTests[1] is read even when aTests is empty, which raises an error. Make the test an :IF and read the value inside it.
15:42-15:60 warning iif_guard_ineffective: IIf evaluates both value arguments, so oOwner:displayName is read even when oOwner is NIL, which raises an error. Make the test an :IF and read the value inside it.
